---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import { path } from '../../i18n/routes';
import { CONTACT_EMAIL } from '../../config/site';
---
<Base lang="en" page="about" title="About" description="Why Plan My Cinema exists: home cinema calculators sharing one room model, with sources instead of rules of thumb – built while planning a real home cinema.">
  <article class="prose">
    <h1 class="page-head">About</h1>

    <h2>Why this site exists</h2>
    <p>
      I built a home cinema myself. The hardest part wasn't the construction – it was finding reliable numbers. Throw distances and lens shift hide
      in data sheets, speaker angles in Dolby's guidelines, room modes in acoustics textbooks, and every online calculator asked for the room
      dimensions all over again. Much of it only existed as a rule of thumb with no source behind it.
    </p>
    <p>
      Plan My Cinema is what I wished I'd had back then: enter your room once, and every calculator works with the same dimensions, the same seats
      and the same equipment.
    </p>

    <h2>What the calculators do</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><a href={path('screen', 'en')}>Screen &amp; projection</a>: throw distance, image brightness in nits and fL, lens shift and viewing distance – with a projector list built from manufacturer data.</li>
      <li><a href={path('modes', 'en')}>Room modes</a>: which bass frequencies your room boosts, what reaches each seat, and how subwoofers, an SBA or a DBA change that.</li>
      <li><a href={path('speakers', 'en')}>Speakers</a>: Dolby Atmos layouts with angle checks for every seat, sightlines across rows and where to put absorbers.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>How we work</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Sources, not rules of thumb:</strong> limits and guide values come with their source. Where no binding standard exists, or a threshold is our own choice, we say so.</li>
      <li><strong>Manufacturer data by hand:</strong> projector specs are copied one by one from manufacturer data sheets, not scraped from databases.</li>
      <li><strong>Transparent maths:</strong> every formula is explained. Results are approximations and no substitute for measuring your own room.</li>
      <li><strong>Your data stays with you:</strong> the room is stored only in your browser. No sign-up, no cookies, no tracking.</li>
      <li><strong>Metric first</strong>, with feet and inches on request – the site started in German, English followed.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Questions and suggestions</h2>
    <p>
      Missing a spec, a projector or a topic, or spotted something odd in a result? Write to me at{' '}
      <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>. Questions that matter to many people will find their way into the explanations on the site.
    </p>
    <p>
      I can't offer individual planning advice – there are plenty of home cinema companies happy to help with your build, and Facebook groups
      where your questions will get answered.
    </p>
    <p>
      How we handle your message is described in the <a href={path('privacy', 'en')}>privacy policy</a>.
    </p>
  </article>
</Base>
